ondition: \"DN < 250\", value: \"U0 / D0 (0 x DN upstream, 0 x DN downstream)\"}, {condition: \"DN ≥ 250\", value: \"U3 / D0 (3 x DN upstream, 0 x DN downstream)\"}]}\n  \n  Note: text says \"except for full bore sizes DN250 and larger\". Condition: \"full bore sizes DN250 and larger\" vs \"otherwise\".\n- reverse_flow: \"The sensor is intended to measure reverse flow\" — string true-ish. Value: \"intended to measure reverse flow\". I'll put {value: true}? Hmm, \"Reverse flow: The sensor is intended to measure reverse flow\" → reverse_flow_supported: true. I'll use attribute reverse_flow with value string \"The sensor is intended to measure reverse flow\". Simpler: value: true. I'll go with value: true.\n- pressure_loss_class: config-level by bore size AND bore type. This is complex:\n  Reduced bore:\n  - DN40 & DN50: Δp 40 (0.40 bar)\n  - > DN50: Δp 63 (0.63 bar)\n  (Virtual) Full bore:\n  - DN40 & DN50: Δp 10 (0.10 bar)\n  - DN65–DN200: Δp 16 (0.16 bar)\n  - DN250 and larger: Δp 10 (0.10 bar)\n  \n  config_level: attribute \"pressure_loss_class\", axis \"bore_type / meter_size\", values:\n  - {condition: \"reduced bore, DN40 and DN50\", value: \"Δp 40\", ...} with numeric 0.40 bar? The class is Δp 40 corresponding to 0.40 bar. I can give value \"Δp 40 (0.40 bar)\" as string, or value 0.40 with unit bar and extra field. The structured form allows value string. I'll use value: \"Δp 40\" and add... hmm. Let me structure: attribute pressure_loss_class, values with condition strings like \"Reduced bore, DN40–DN50\", value \"Δp40 (0.40 bar)\". Keep as string since it's a class designation. That's acceptable — value can be string.\n- power supply: three types:\n  - AC mains: 85–240 VAC @ 50/60 Hz →\n    - power_supply_voltage_ac_mains: {min: 85, max: 240} \"V\"\n    - power_supply_frequency: {min: 50, max: 60} \"Hz\"\n    - power_supply_type: \"AC mains\"\n  - Renewable energy (DC powered): 6–32 V →\n    - power_supply_voltage_dc: {min: 6, max: 32} \"V\"\n  - Replaceable